<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Schwarzenberg</h1><p class="st-meta">1670 CE – 1806 CE (approx.) · capital Scheinfeld</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Franconian territory of the Schwarzenberg family, whose princes became some of the greatest landowners and statesmen of the Habsburg monarchy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lords of Seinsheim took the name Schwarzenberg from a castle near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheinfeld">Scheinfeld</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> in the 15th century. In 1599 the family was raised to the rank of imperial counts, and in 1670 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-adolf-i-prince-of-schwarzenberg">Johann Adolf von Schwarzenberg</a>, a senior adviser of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-i-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Leopold</a> I, was made a prince of the Empire, with the lands around Scheinfeld forming the core of the family's immediate territory.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Franconian lands were small, but the family's real weight lay in service to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and in vast estates acquired in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hluboka-nad-vltavou">Frauenberg</a> (Hluboká), bought in 1661, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesky-krumlov">Krumau</a> (Český Krumlov), inherited from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-eggenberg">Eggenberg</a> family in 1719. The territory was Catholic and administered by officials while the princes lived at court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> or on their Bohemian estates.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1806 the Franconian lands were mediatised and placed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria</a>. The family remained prominent: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-philipp-prince-of-schwarzenberg">Karl Philipp zu Schwarzenberg</a> commanded the allied armies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in 1813, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-zu-schwarzenberg">Felix zu Schwarzenberg</a> led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire's</a> government after the 1848 revolution.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1670 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.94%;width:2.71%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1670 CE – 1806 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Scheinfeld</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Johann Adolf I, Adam Franz, Joseph Johann Nepomuk</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schwarzenberg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=principality-of-schwarzenberg" aria-label="Principality of Schwarzenberg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4920 448 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Schwarzenberg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5240 704L5229 694M5240 704L5269 749M5240 704L5197 764"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5269 749h0M5197 764h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5240 704h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5240 704h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Scheinfeld. <a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=principality-of-schwarzenberg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
